  "id": "COMPOUND:11770 - PROTEIN:585",
  "verbalization": "Relcovaptan is implicated in the pathway leading to Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Relcovaptan directly targets C-C motif chemokine 8, which is a target of specionin and also of dexamethasone. Dexamethasone, in turn, has a target relationship with Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase, while C-C motif chemokine 8 is involved in a more complex pathway that ultimately leads to the same enzyme. This indicates that Relcovaptan may influence Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate dehydrogenase through a multi-step mechanism involving chemokine signaling and steroid hormone interactions. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Relcovaptan to modulate metabolic processes via indirect pathways, suggesting a broader role in cellular metabolism and signaling.",
